{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"./events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"events stream"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is what a "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"client"}]},{"type":"text","value":" reads. This page is the\n"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server-side"}]},{"type":"text","value":" half: hooks that fire on every file the agent touches, sandbox\ndebug logging, and the low-level watcher you can drive outside a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" run."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"file-event-hooks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"File-event hooks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Listen to files being created, changed or deleted inside a sandbox, for\nexample to watch what the agent edits as it works. The watcher is\nprovider-agnostic: it uses native OS watching where the provider supports it\n(local-process) and falls back to a portable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"find"},{"type":"text","value":" poll everywhere else (Docker\nand other exec-only providers), with no extra dependencies or image changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are two places to declare these hooks, with different scopes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sandbox-scoped-hooks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandbox-scoped hooks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Declared directly on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineSandbox({ hooks })"},{"type":"text","value":". They fire "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"once per file\nevent"}]},{"type":"text","value":", regardless of how many runs share the sandbox, alongside the sandbox's\nown lifecycle callbacks:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'repo-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  hooks: {\n    // catch-all: fires for every event\n    onFile: (e) => console.log(`[${e.type}] ${e.path}`),\n    // type-specific variants\n    onFileCreate: (e) => console.log('created', e.path),\n    onFileChange: (e) => console.log('changed', e.path),\n    onFileDelete: (e) => console.log('deleted', e.path),\n    // lifecycle\n    onReady: (handle) => console.log('sandbox ready', handle.id),\n    onError: (err) => console.error('sandbox error', err),\n    onDestroy: () => console.log('sandbox destroyed'),\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"run-scoped-hooks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run-scoped hooks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To handle file events inside a middleware (for example per-request audit\nlogging), use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":" hook group on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineChatMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":". These fire\n"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per-run"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and each handler receives the current run's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddlewareContext"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nconst auditMiddleware = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: 'audit',\n  // ctx is the ChatMiddlewareContext for the current run\n  sandbox: {\n    onFile: (ctx, e) => console.log(ctx.runId, e.type, e.path),\n    onFileCreate: (ctx, e) => db.log({ run: ctx.runId, event: e }),\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both hook groups fire "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server-side"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and are independent of the stream: the\nengine automatically emits one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"./events#custom-events","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nevent per change regardless of whether you register any hooks, so the client\ncan react to the same edits without extra middleware."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reading-content-and-diffs-in-hooks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reading content and diffs in hooks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The event every hook receives is more than "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type, path, timestamp }"},{"type":"text","value":". It also\ncarries lazy, git-backed accessors for the file's content:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface SandboxFileHookEvent {\n  type: \"create\" | \"change\" | \"delete\";\n  path: string;\n  timestamp: number;\n  before(): Promise<string>; // content at the session baseline ('' if new / non-git)\n  after(): Promise<string>; // current content ('' if deleted)\n  diff(): Promise<string>; // unified patch vs the baseline\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reach for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diff()"},{"type":"text","value":" to show what the agent changed. There is no need to hand-roll a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff"},{"type":"text","value":" yourself:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\n\nconst repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-agent\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  hooks: {\n    onFileChange: async (e) => {\n      const patch = await e.diff();\n      console.log(`${e.path} changed:\\n${patch}`);\n    },\n  },\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same accessors are available on run-scoped hooks, where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"e"},{"type":"text","value":" is the\nsecond argument:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst auditMiddleware = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"audit\",\n  sandbox: {\n    onFileChange: async (ctx, e) => {\n      const [before, after] = await Promise.all([e.before(), e.after()]);\n      db.log({ run: ctx.runId, path: e.path, before, after });\n    },\n  },\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lazy, path-only hooks pay nothing."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"before()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"after()"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diff()"},{"type":"text","value":"\nare methods, not fields: each one only reads the file or shells out to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git"},{"type":"text","value":"\nwhen you call it. A hook that only reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"e.path"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"e.type"},{"type":"text","value":" (like the\ncatch-all logger in "},{"type":"link","href":"#sandbox-scoped-hooks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandbox-scoped hooks"}]},{"type":"text","value":" above)\nnever touches the filesystem or spawns a process."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Git session baseline."}]},{"type":"text","value":" At "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onReady"},{"type":"text","value":", the sandbox snapshots\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git rev-parse HEAD"},{"type":"text","value":" once, as the session's baseline commit (empty if the\nworkspace isn't a git repo, or has no commits yet). Every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"before()"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diff()"},{"type":"text","value":" call for the rest of the session diffs against that same fixed\nbaseline, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFileChange"},{"type":"text","value":" always reports the file's "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"cumulative"}]},{"type":"text","value":" change\nsince the run started, not just the delta since the watcher's last poll.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"after()"},{"type":"text","value":" always reads the file's current on-disk content, independent of\nthe baseline. None of the three accessors throw: a deleted file resolves\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"after()"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"''"},{"type":"text","value":" (it still has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"before()"},{"type":"text","value":"); a new file resolves "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"before()"},{"type":"text","value":"\nto "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"''"},{"type":"text","value":" (it still has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"after()"},{"type":"text","value":"); a non-git workspace resolves "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"both"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"before()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"after()"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"''"},{"type":"text","value":" and makes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diff()"},{"type":"text","value":" fall back to a\nsynthesized add-patch built from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"after()"},{"type":"text","value":", except for a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"},{"type":"text","value":" event in\na non-git workspace, where there's nothing to synthesize and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diff()"},{"type":"text","value":"\nresolves to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"''"},{"type":"text","value":". In a git workspace, a file git "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"is not tracking yet"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (one the\nagent just created) and every later edit to it diff empty because\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff"},{"type":"text","value":" ignores untracked files, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diff()"},{"type":"text","value":" falls back to that same\nsynthesized add-patch whenever the file is absent at the baseline. A file the\nagent creates (and keeps editing) therefore never streams an empty diff, while\na "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tracked"}]},{"type":"text","value":" file that's identical to the baseline correctly stays empty.\nA "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"git-ignored"}]},{"type":"text","value":" file (e.g. a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" or a credentials file) is the exception:\nthe file event still fires so you're notified it changed, but "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diff()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"''"},{"type":"text","value":" so its contents are never surfaced in the diff feed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every git, exec and fs failure behind these accessors, and behind the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"find"},{"type":"text","value":"-poll\nwatcher, still falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"''"},{"type":"text","value":" (or preserves the last snapshot), but is\n"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"logged first"}]},{"type":"text","value":" so a failure is observable rather than a silent empty value:\nreal anomalies (a failed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff"},{"type":"text","value":", an unreadable file, a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"find"},{"type":"text","value":" poll that\nexits non-zero, a lost git baseline) under the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errors"},{"type":"text","value":" category (on by\ndefault), and expected-empty conditions (a new file's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"before()"},{"type":"text","value":") under the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":" debug category. Enable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debug: { sandbox: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" (see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"#debugging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging"}]},{"type":"text","value":") to see the latter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"disabling-file-watching","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disabling file watching"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To stop the watcher and suppress "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file"},{"type":"text","value":" events for a sandbox entirely,\nset "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileEvents: false"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'quiet-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  fileEvents: false, // watcher not started; no sandbox.file events emitted\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"debugging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To log sandbox internals (watcher start and stop, event dispatch, lifecycle\ntransitions) pass the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":" debug category to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { repoSandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nchat({\n  threadId: 'thread-1',\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(repoSandbox)],\n  debug: { sandbox: true }, // or `debug: true` for all categories\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"low-level-watchworkspace","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Low-level: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchWorkspace()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchWorkspace()"},{"type":"text","value":" is the building block the hooks are built on. Reach for it\nwhen you want the watcher "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"outside"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" run:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { watchWorkspace } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { repoSandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst handle = await repoSandbox.ensure({ threadId: 'thread-1', runId: 'run-1' })\nconst watcher = await watchWorkspace(handle, {\n  onEvent: (event) => {\n    // event.type is 'create' | 'change' | 'delete'\n    console.log(`${event.type} ${event.path}`)\n  },\n  ignore: ['.git', 'node_modules'], // default\n})\n// …do work outside a chat run…\nawait watcher.stop()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Events"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" event stream the client reads."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle & Snapshots"}]},{"type":"text","value":": when sandboxes are created and torn down."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":": bridged host tools that surface as tool-call chunks."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"file-event-hooks","text":"File-event hooks","level":2},{"id":"sandbox-scoped-hooks","text":"Sandbox-scoped hooks","level":3},{"id":"run-scoped-hooks","text":"Run-scoped hooks","level":3},{"id":"reading-content-and-diffs-in-hooks","text":"Reading content and diffs in hooks","level":2},{"id":"disabling-file-watching","text":"Disabling file watching","level":2},{"id":"debugging","text":"Debugging","level":2},{"id":"low-level-watchworkspace","text":"Low-level: watchWorkspace()","level":2},{"id":"related","text":"Related","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe [events stream](./events) is what a *client* reads. This page is the\n*server-side* half: hooks that fire on every file the agent touches, sandbox\ndebug logging, and the low-level watcher you can drive outside a `chat()` run.\n\n## File-event hooks\n\nListen to files being created, changed or deleted inside a sandbox, for\nexample to watch what the agent edits as it works. The watcher is\nprovider-agnostic: it uses native OS watching where the provider supports it\n(local-process) and falls back to a portable `find` poll everywhere else (Docker\nand other exec-only providers), with no extra dependencies or image changes.\n\nThere are two places to declare these hooks, with different scopes.\n\n### Sandbox-scoped hooks\n\nDeclared directly on `defineSandbox({ hooks })`. They fire **once per file\nevent**, regardless of how many runs share the sandbox, alongside the sandbox's\nown lifecycle callbacks:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'repo-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  hooks: {\n    // catch-all: fires for every event\n    onFile: (e) => console.log(`[${e.type}] ${e.path}`),\n    // type-specific variants\n    onFileCreate: (e) => console.log('created', e.path),\n    onFileChange: (e) => console.log('changed', e.path),\n    onFileDelete: (e) => console.log('deleted', e.path),\n    // lifecycle\n    onReady: (handle) => console.log('sandbox ready', handle.id),\n    onError: (err) => console.error('sandbox error', err),\n    onDestroy: () => console.log('sandbox destroyed'),\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Run-scoped hooks\n\nTo handle file events inside a middleware (for example per-request audit\nlogging), use the `sandbox` hook group on `defineChatMiddleware`. These fire\n**per-run**, and each handler receives the current run's `ChatMiddlewareContext`:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nconst auditMiddleware = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: 'audit',\n  // ctx is the ChatMiddlewareContext for the current run\n  sandbox: {\n    onFile: (ctx, e) => console.log(ctx.runId, e.type, e.path),\n    onFileCreate: (ctx, e) => db.log({ run: ctx.runId, event: e }),\n  },\n})\n```\n\nBoth hook groups fire **server-side** and are independent of the stream: the\nengine automatically emits one `CUSTOM` [`sandbox.file`](./events#custom-events)\nevent per change regardless of whether you register any hooks, so the client\ncan react to the same edits without extra middleware.\n\n## Reading content and diffs in hooks\n\nThe event every hook receives is more than `{ type, path, timestamp }`. It also\ncarries lazy, git-backed accessors for the file's content:\n\n```ts\ninterface SandboxFileHookEvent {\n  type: \"create\" | \"change\" | \"delete\";\n  path: string;\n  timestamp: number;\n  before(): Promise<string>; // content at the session baseline ('' if new / non-git)\n  after(): Promise<string>; // current content ('' if deleted)\n  diff(): Promise<string>; // unified patch vs the baseline\n}\n```\n\nReach for `diff()` to show what the agent changed. There is no need to hand-roll a\n`git diff` yourself:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\n\nconst repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-agent\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  hooks: {\n    onFileChange: async (e) => {\n      const patch = await e.diff();\n      console.log(`${e.path} changed:\\n${patch}`);\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\nThe same accessors are available on run-scoped hooks, where `e` is the\nsecond argument:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst auditMiddleware = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"audit\",\n  sandbox: {\n    onFileChange: async (ctx, e) => {\n      const [before, after] = await Promise.all([e.before(), e.after()]);\n      db.log({ run: ctx.runId, path: e.path, before, after });\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n**Lazy, path-only hooks pay nothing.** `before()`, `after()`, and `diff()`\nare methods, not fields: each one only reads the file or shells out to `git`\nwhen you call it. A hook that only reads `e.path` / `e.type` (like the\ncatch-all logger in [Sandbox-scoped hooks](#sandbox-scoped-hooks) above)\nnever touches the filesystem or spawns a process.\n\n**Git session baseline.** At `onReady`, the sandbox snapshots\n`git rev-parse HEAD` once, as the session's baseline commit (empty if the\nworkspace isn't a git repo, or has no commits yet). Every `before()` and\n`diff()` call for the rest of the session diffs against that same fixed\nbaseline, so `onFileChange` always reports the file's **cumulative** change\nsince the run started, not just the delta since the watcher's last poll.\n`after()` always reads the file's current on-disk content, independent of\nthe baseline. None of the three accessors throw: a deleted file resolves\n`after()` to `''` (it still has `before()`); a new file resolves `before()`\nto `''` (it still has `after()`); a non-git workspace resolves **both**\n`before()` and `after()` to `''` and makes `diff()` fall back to a\nsynthesized add-patch built from `after()`, except for a `delete` event in\na non-git workspace, where there's nothing to synthesize and `diff()`\nresolves to `''`. In a git workspace, a file git **is not tracking yet** (one the\nagent just created) and every later edit to it diff empty because\n`git diff` ignores untracked files, so `diff()` falls back to that same\nsynthesized add-patch whenever the file is absent at the baseline. A file the\nagent creates (and keeps editing) therefore never streams an empty diff, while\na **tracked** file that's identical to the baseline correctly stays empty.\nA **git-ignored** file (e.g. a `.env` or a credentials file) is the exception:\nthe file event still fires so you're notified it changed, but `diff()` returns\n`''` so its contents are never surfaced in the diff feed.\n\nEvery git, exec and fs failure behind these accessors, and behind the `find`-poll\nwatcher, still falls back to `''` (or preserves the last snapshot), but is\n**logged first** so a failure is observable rather than a silent empty value:\nreal anomalies (a failed `git diff`, an unreadable file, a `find` poll that\nexits non-zero, a lost git baseline) under the `errors` category (on by\ndefault), and expected-empty conditions (a new file's `before()`) under the\n`sandbox` debug category. Enable `debug: { sandbox: true }` (see\n[Debugging](#debugging)) to see the latter.\n\n## Disabling file watching\n\nTo stop the watcher and suppress `sandbox.file` events for a sandbox entirely,\nset `fileEvents: false`:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'quiet-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  fileEvents: false, // watcher not started; no sandbox.file events emitted\n})\n```\n\n## Debugging\n\nTo log sandbox internals (watcher start and stop, event dispatch, lifecycle\ntransitions) pass the `sandbox` debug category to `chat()`:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { repoSandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nchat({\n  threadId: 'thread-1',\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(repoSandbox)],\n  debug: { sandbox: true }, // or `debug: true` for all categories\n})\n```\n\n## Low-level: `watchWorkspace()`\n\n`watchWorkspace()` is the building block the hooks are built on. Reach for it\nwhen you want the watcher **outside** a `chat()` run:\n\n```ts\nimport { watchWorkspace } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { repoSandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst handle = await repoSandbox.ensure({ threadId: 'thread-1', runId: 'run-1' })\nconst watcher = await watchWorkspace(handle, {\n  onEvent: (event) => {\n    // event.type is 'create' | 'change' | 'delete'\n    console.log(`${event.type} ${event.path}`)\n  },\n  ignore: ['.git', 'node_modules'], // default\n})\n// …do work outside a chat run…\nawait watcher.stop()\n```\n\n## Related\n\n- [Events](./events): the `CUSTOM` event stream the client reads.\n- [Lifecycle & Snapshots](./lifecycle): when sandboxes are created and torn down.\n- [Tools](./tools): bridged host tools that surface as tool-call chunks.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Observability (Advanced)\nid: observability\norder: 10\ndescription: \"Run server-side hooks on every file the agent touches, log sandbox internals, and watch a workspace outside a chat() run.\"\n---\n\nThe [events stream](./events) is what a *client* reads. This page is the\n*server-side* half: hooks that fire on every file the agent touches, sandbox\ndebug logging, and the low-level watcher you can drive outside a `chat()` run.\n\n## File-event hooks\n\nListen to files being created, changed or deleted inside a sandbox, for\nexample to watch what the agent edits as it works. The watcher is\nprovider-agnostic: it uses native OS watching where the provider supports it\n(local-process) and falls back to a portable `find` poll everywhere else (Docker\nand other exec-only providers), with no extra dependencies or image changes.\n\nThere are two places to declare these hooks, with different scopes.\n\n### Sandbox-scoped hooks\n\nDeclared directly on `defineSandbox({ hooks })`. They fire **once per file\nevent**, regardless of how many runs share the sandbox, alongside the sandbox's\nown lifecycle callbacks:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'repo-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  hooks: {\n    // catch-all: fires for every event\n    onFile: (e) => console.log(`[${e.type}] ${e.path}`),\n    // type-specific variants\n    onFileCreate: (e) => console.log('created', e.path),\n    onFileChange: (e) => console.log('changed', e.path),\n    onFileDelete: (e) => console.log('deleted', e.path),\n    // lifecycle\n    onReady: (handle) => console.log('sandbox ready', handle.id),\n    onError: (err) => console.error('sandbox error', err),\n    onDestroy: () => console.log('sandbox destroyed'),\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Run-scoped hooks\n\nTo handle file events inside a middleware (for example per-request audit\nlogging), use the `sandbox` hook group on `defineChatMiddleware`. These fire\n**per-run**, and each handler receives the current run's `ChatMiddlewareContext`:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nconst auditMiddleware = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: 'audit',\n  // ctx is the ChatMiddlewareContext for the current run\n  sandbox: {\n    onFile: (ctx, e) => console.log(ctx.runId, e.type, e.path),\n    onFileCreate: (ctx, e) => db.log({ run: ctx.runId, event: e }),\n  },\n})\n```\n\nBoth hook groups fire **server-side** and are independent of the stream: the\nengine automatically emits one `CUSTOM` [`sandbox.file`](./events#custom-events)\nevent per change regardless of whether you register any hooks, so the client\ncan react to the same edits without extra middleware.\n\n## Reading content and diffs in hooks\n\nThe event every hook receives is more than `{ type, path, timestamp }`. It also\ncarries lazy, git-backed accessors for the file's content:\n\n```ts\ninterface SandboxFileHookEvent {\n  type: \"create\" | \"change\" | \"delete\";\n  path: string;\n  timestamp: number;\n  before(): Promise<string>; // content at the session baseline ('' if new / non-git)\n  after(): Promise<string>; // current content ('' if deleted)\n  diff(): Promise<string>; // unified patch vs the baseline\n}\n```\n\nReach for `diff()` to show what the agent changed. There is no need to hand-roll a\n`git diff` yourself:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\n\nconst repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-agent\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  hooks: {\n    onFileChange: async (e) => {\n      const patch = await e.diff();\n      console.log(`${e.path} changed:\\n${patch}`);\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\nThe same accessors are available on run-scoped hooks, where `e` is the\nsecond argument:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChatMiddleware } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst auditMiddleware = defineChatMiddleware({\n  name: \"audit\",\n  sandbox: {\n    onFileChange: async (ctx, e) => {\n      const [before, after] = await Promise.all([e.before(), e.after()]);\n      db.log({ run: ctx.runId, path: e.path, before, after });\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n**Lazy, path-only hooks pay nothing.** `before()`, `after()`, and `diff()`\nare methods, not fields: each one only reads the file or shells out to `git`\nwhen you call it. A hook that only reads `e.path` / `e.type` (like the\ncatch-all logger in [Sandbox-scoped hooks](#sandbox-scoped-hooks) above)\nnever touches the filesystem or spawns a process.\n\n**Git session baseline.** At `onReady`, the sandbox snapshots\n`git rev-parse HEAD` once, as the session's baseline commit (empty if the\nworkspace isn't a git repo, or has no commits yet). Every `before()` and\n`diff()` call for the rest of the session diffs against that same fixed\nbaseline, so `onFileChange` always reports the file's **cumulative** change\nsince the run started, not just the delta since the watcher's last poll.\n`after()` always reads the file's current on-disk content, independent of\nthe baseline. None of the three accessors throw: a deleted file resolves\n`after()` to `''` (it still has `before()`); a new file resolves `before()`\nto `''` (it still has `after()`); a non-git workspace resolves **both**\n`before()` and `after()` to `''` and makes `diff()` fall back to a\nsynthesized add-patch built from `after()`, except for a `delete` event in\na non-git workspace, where there's nothing to synthesize and `diff()`\nresolves to `''`. In a git workspace, a file git **is not tracking yet** (one the\nagent just created) and every later edit to it diff empty because\n`git diff` ignores untracked files, so `diff()` falls back to that same\nsynthesized add-patch whenever the file is absent at the baseline. A file the\nagent creates (and keeps editing) therefore never streams an empty diff, while\na **tracked** file that's identical to the baseline correctly stays empty.\nA **git-ignored** file (e.g. a `.env` or a credentials file) is the exception:\nthe file event still fires so you're notified it changed, but `diff()` returns\n`''` so its contents are never surfaced in the diff feed.\n\nEvery git, exec and fs failure behind these accessors, and behind the `find`-poll\nwatcher, still falls back to `''` (or preserves the last snapshot), but is\n**logged first** so a failure is observable rather than a silent empty value:\nreal anomalies (a failed `git diff`, an unreadable file, a `find` poll that\nexits non-zero, a lost git baseline) under the `errors` category (on by\ndefault), and expected-empty conditions (a new file's `before()`) under the\n`sandbox` debug category. Enable `debug: { sandbox: true }` (see\n[Debugging](#debugging)) to see the latter.\n\n## Disabling file watching\n\nTo stop the watcher and suppress `sandbox.file` events for a sandbox entirely,\nset `fileEvents: false`:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'quiet-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  fileEvents: false, // watcher not started; no sandbox.file events emitted\n})\n```\n\n## Debugging\n\nTo log sandbox internals (watcher start and stop, event dispatch, lifecycle\ntransitions) pass the `sandbox` debug category to `chat()`:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { repoSandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nchat({\n  threadId: 'thread-1',\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(repoSandbox)],\n  debug: { sandbox: true }, // or `debug: true` for all categories\n})\n```\n\n## Low-level: `watchWorkspace()`\n\n`watchWorkspace()` is the building block the hooks are built on. Reach for it\nwhen you want the watcher **outside** a `chat()` run:\n\n```ts\nimport { watchWorkspace } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { repoSandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst handle = await repoSandbox.ensure({ threadId: 'thread-1', runId: 'run-1' })\nconst watcher = await watchWorkspace(handle, {\n  onEvent: (event) => {\n    // event.type is 'create' | 'change' | 'delete'\n    console.log(`${event.type} ${event.path}`)\n  },\n  ignore: ['.git', 'node_modules'], // default\n})\n// …do work outside a chat run…\nawait watcher.stop()\n```\n\n## Related\n\n- [Events](./events): the `CUSTOM` event stream the client reads.\n- [Lifecycle & Snapshots](./lifecycle): when sandboxes are created and torn down.\n- [Tools](./tools): bridged host tools that surface as tool-call chunks.\n"}
